From: Michael Stufflebeam <cpuchip@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:48:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Babal at stu32-arcade 599c510: its keys by APP_KEY_*, its
 seed from app_seed() (apps.h v1.2)

Babal names its keys by app_keys.h and seeds each game from app_seed() (the hardware RNG here),
folded into the game count and the start key's ms, so levels no longer repeat across power cycles.
Same frames otherwise. At stu32-arcade: appcheck (9 scripts identical to babalcore and the spec,
app-far reaching row 126, every plant red), and on the S3 in soroban's window (#4899) 22,641 frames
hashing as on the host, the control red.

Checked on 7776c7c in a scratch clone (GAMES_REPOS and CASIM_REPO set to the local clones): make all
and make test pass (app_test 625/625, standin_test 349/349, the generator test green); the stand-in
and Rev A images build, Babal's 18 files with the frame guard and -ffp-contract=off (casim.c has the
guard of its own).

Written by arcade for soroban's gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 games.list | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/games.list b/games.list
